{
  "_comment": [
    "Canonical Bulgarian sidebar label of every round (presentation overlay; the paper JSON is hash-bound to its receipt and is never edited to fix a label).",
    "rounds[competition]['<raw paper.round>|<paper.roundType>'] -> label ('' for a null round: '|theory'). papers[paperId] -> label, for the raw combinations that mix several events (checked paper by paper against its masthead). grades[competition][raw grade] -> grade label, where the generic rule (9 -> '9. клас', 9-10 -> '9–10 клас', physics ST/SP -> 'Специална тема', astronomy ML/ST -> 'Младша/Старша възраст') is wrong or uneven for that competition; '' drops a grade that is not one (IPhO '8-9' is the file date 2012-08-09, IOAA 2021 '9' is Q9). suffixes[paperId] -> text appended after the grade, for papers of one round and grade that are different sittings or copies: 'първи ден' / 'втори ден', 'тест', 'вариант 2', 'лист 1', 'друг препис' (the same exam transcribed from a second archive file).",
    "A sidebar node is labelled '<round label> · <grade label> · <suffix>'; the raw paper.title is never a label. Resolved by scripts/lib/navigation.mjs (pages) and src/problems/tree.ts (sidebar); scripts/check-navigation.mjs fails on a paper this file does not label.",
    "Rules. One event -> one label, whatever the raw spelling (theory / Theo / Practical Round / observational / Prac; II / II кръг (областен); regional / Региональный этап).",
    "International olympiads whose papers are one file per question or per tour get the tour label: Теория, Експеримент, Наблюдения, Анализ на данни, Практически тур, Отборен тур, Тест; a whole olympiad in one file (IPhO 1968-1976) is 'Теория и експеримент'. A practical round made of data-analysis problems stays 'Практически тур' (IAO, OWAO).",
    "Bulgarian national rounds keep their full form ('III кръг (национален)'); a bare numeral ('III') takes the full form its siblings in that competition use; a round printed otherwise keeps its printed qualifier ('I кръг (училищен)', 'III кръг (регионален)'). НЕСФ and НПСФ hold one round a year: their label is '' and the node is named by the grade alone.",
    "Russian and Belarusian stages in Bulgarian: Районен етап, Областен етап, Регионален етап, Заключителен етап. Training camps: 'Летен/Есенен/Зимен сбор', 'Сбор N'. Tournaments (IYPT, IYNT): 'Задачи на турнира'.",
    "Papers of one year that share a label and a language merge into one sidebar node when their display numbers (content/question-numbers.json) do not collide. An original and its translation are split by language ('· на английски', '· на български'); colliding papers are split by tour ('· теория', '· тест') unless the round label already names the tour; a suffix here settles what is left (check-navigation.mjs warns about a node told apart only by its paper id).",
    "Nikola and the null-round VsOA-ru / ПУ / USAAAO / НОА papers have no combination entry on purpose (НОА '|theory' was the 1998-1999 booklet of several rounds, now labelled in papers[]): those raw combinations mix events, so a new paper there must get its own label before it ships."
  ],
